      sections: [{"id":"s1","title":"Finding Your Balance","whyItMatters":"Typing too fast with low accuracy is slower overall. Controlled speed with high accuracy wins.","content":"**The Speed-Accuracy Curve:**\n- Speed increases → accuracy drops initially\n- With practice, both rise together\n- Plateau phase: push speed, accuracy dips, then recovers\n\n**Controlled Practice Method:**\n1. Type at comfortable speed for 5 min\n2. Note accuracy and WPM\n3. Increase speed by 5%\n4. If accuracy drops below 90%, slow down\n5. Repeat daily\n\n**The 90% Rule:** Never type faster than your 90% accuracy pace.\n\n**Real Math:**\n80 WPM at 95% = 76 correct WPM\n100 WPM at 80% = 80 correct WPM — feels faster but same output","codeExamples":[{"id":"ex1","title":"Balance Drill","description":"Speed vs accuracy practice","code":{"typing-speed":"practice makes perfect progress not perfection\ntype slowly with care then gradually increase\nspeed will come with time and consistent effort\nfocus on accuracy not speed speed follows"},"explanation":"Type these proverbs at a pace where you maintain 90%+ accuracy."}]}],
