      sections: [{"id":"s1","title":"Building Muscle Memory","whyItMatters":"Muscle memory makes typing automatic, freeing your brain for content and coding logic.","content":"**How Muscle Memory Forms:**\n1. Cognitive Stage: Consciously think about each finger\n2. Associative Stage: Patterns begin to feel natural\n3. Autonomous Stage: Fingers move without thinking\n\n**Spaced Repetition for Typing:**\n- Day 1: 20 min practice\n- Day 2: 15 min review + 5 min new\n- Day 4: 10 min review\n- Day 7: 5 min review\n- Day 14: Quick warm-up\n\n**Practice Structure:**\n- 5 min: Warm-up (home row)\n- 10 min: Targeted drills\n- 5 min: Speed test\n- 5 min: Review errors\n\n**Neuroplasticity:** The brain rewires itself with repetition. ~21 days of daily practice builds lasting pathways.","codeExamples":[{"id":"ex1","title":"Muscle Memory Builder","description":"Daily practice routine","code":{"typing-speed":"asdf jkl; asdf jkl; asdf jkl;\nqaz wsx edc rfv tgb tgbrfv\nyhn ujm ik, ol. p;/ ;/.ol ik, ujm yhn\nthe quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog\nthe five boxing wizards jump quickly"},"explanation":"Follow the warm-up → drill → test → review structure."}]}],
