      sections: [{"id":"s1","title":"Ergonomic Setup","whyItMatters":"Poor posture leads to repetitive strain injury (RSI), which can permanently end your typing career.","content":"**Desk Setup:**\n- Elbows at 90°, forearms parallel to floor\n- Wrists straight (not bent up/down)\n- Keyboard at or slightly below elbow height\n- Monitor at arm's length, top at eye level\n\n**Chair:**\n- Feet flat on floor\n- Thighs parallel to ground\n- Lumbar support engaged\n- Seat height so knees at 90°\n\n**Typing Posture:**\n- Sit up straight, shoulders relaxed\n- Wrists floating (not resting on desk)\n- Fingers curved, hovering over home row\n- No wrist extension (bending back)\n\n**Break Schedule (Pomodoro for Typing):**\n- 25 min typing → 5 min break\n- Every 2 hours → 15 min break\n- Stretch fingers, wrists, shoulders\n\n**Warning Signs:**\n- Numbness/tingling in fingers\n- Wrist pain after typing\n- Forearm tightness\n- Take action early!","codeExamples":[{"id":"ex1","title":"Posture Check","description":"Type this while checking your posture","code":{"typing-speed":"I am sitting up straight with feet flat on floor\nMy wrists are straight and fingers are curved\nElbows are at 90 degrees and shoulders relaxed\nMonitor is at eye level and I am taking breaks"},"explanation":"Read and check each line against your actual posture."}]}],
