      sections: [{"id":"s1","title":"Error Analysis","whyItMatters":"Most typists repeat the same 5-10 errors 80% of the time. Fixing these patterns dramatically improves accuracy.","content":"**Common Error Types:**\n1. Transposition: 'teh' → 'the', 'recieve' → 'receive'\n2. Doubling: 'acccident' instead of 'accident'\n3. Adjacent: 'q' pressed instead of 'w'\n4. Row slip: '2' instead of 'w' (reaching too far)\n5. Hand confusion: 'b' with right hand instead of left\n\n**Error Log Method:**\n1. Type a paragraph freely\n2. Circle every mistake\n3. Identify the pattern (e.g., left ring finger weak)\n4. Do 20 targeted reps of correct form\n5. Retest\n\n**Correction Drills:**\n- For transposition: Type pairs slowly: teh→the, teh→the\n- For adjacent: Type the row repeatedly\n- For weak fingers: Isolation drills","codeExamples":[{"id":"ex1","title":"Error Correction","description":"Target common error patterns","code":{"typing-speed":"the the the the the the (not teh)\nreceive receive receive receive (not recieve)\naccident accident accident accident (not acccident)\nneighbor neighbor neighbor neighbor (not neightbour)\nseparate separate separate separate (not seperate)"},"explanation":"Type each correct spelling 5x to overwrite the incorrect muscle memory."}]}],
