      sections: [{"id":"s1","title":"CSS Typing Patterns","whyItMatters":"CSS uses { } and : extensively. Mastering these symbols is critical for front-end developers.","content":"**Key Positions:**\n- { (left curly): Right pinkie\n- } (right curly): Right pinkie, shift + ]\n- : (colon): Right pinkie, shift + ;\n- ; (semicolon): Right pinkie\n- # (hash): Left ring, shift + 3\n- . (dot/period): Right ring\n\n**CSS Rule Pattern:**\n`selector { property: value; }`\n\n**Typing Rhythm:**\n1. Type selector\n2. Type { } with space inside\n3. Type property:\n4. Type value;\n5. Type closing }\n\n**Common Patterns:**\n- Class selectors: `.class-name { }`\n- ID selectors: `#id-name { }`\n- Nested: `.parent .child { }`\n- Pseudo: `:hover`, `:before`, `:nth-child()`","codeExamples":[{"id":"ex1","title":"CSS Typing","description":"Practice CSS rule structures","code":{"typing-speed":".container { margin: 0 auto; padding: 20px; }\n#header { background: #333; color: #fff; }\ndiv.main > p:hover { text-decoration: underline; }\n@media (max-width: 768px) { .flex { display: block; } }"},"explanation":"Type each rule focusing on the { : ; } rhythm pattern."}]}],
      quiz: { questions: [{"id":"q1","type":"mcq","question":"Which finger types the { (left curly brace)?","options":["Left ring","Right pinkie","Right index","Left pinkie"],"correctAnswer":"Right pinkie","explanation":"{ is typed with right pinkie (shift + [).","difficulty":2}], passingScore: 70 },
      cheatSheet: [{"label":"{ }","value":"Right pinkie, shift + [ and ]"},{"label":":","value":"Right pinkie, shift + ;"},{"label":"Selector Pattern","value":"selector { property: value; }"}]
