      id: "ts-20", number: 20, title: "Python Syntax Training", subtitle: "Indentation, colons, underscores, and special syntax", difficulty: "Intermediate", estimatedMinutes: 50, xpReward: 60, prerequisites: [], learningObjectives: ["Type Python indentation smoothly", "Master colon and underscore keys", "Handle function and class definitions"], partLabel: "Part 3: Coding Typing Systems",
      sections: [{"id":"s1","title":"Python Typing Patterns","whyItMatters":"Python's syntax relies on indentation and colons rather than braces — a unique typing challenge.","content":"**Key Patterns:**\n- : (colon): Ends function/class/loop headers\n- _ (underscore): Snake_case naming\n- # (hash): Comments\n- ** : Exponentiation\n- // : Floor division\n- def : Function definition\n- class : Class definition\n\n**Python Rhythms:**\n`def function_name(param1, param2):`\n`    return value`\n\n**Indentation Challenge:**\n- Must use consistent spaces (usually 4)\n- Tab key moves cursor, then type code\n- Use shift+tab for dedent\n\n**Common Typing Issues:**\n- Forgetting colon at end of header\n- Mixing tabs and spaces\n- Missing underscores in long names\n- Wrong indentation level","codeExamples":[{"id":"ex1","title":"Python Typing","description":"Practice Python syntax structures","code":{"typing-speed":"def calculate_total(items, tax_rate):\n    total = sum(items)\n    return total * (1 + tax_rate)\n\nclass ShoppingCart:\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.items = []\n\n    def add_item(self, name, price):\n        self.items.append({\"name\": name, \"price\": price})"},"explanation":"Focus on colon placement and consistent 4-space indentation."}]}],
      quiz: { questions: [{"id":"q1","type":"mcq","question":"What character ends Python function headers?","options":[";",":","{","->"],"correctAnswer":":","explanation":"Python uses colon (:) at the end of function/class/loop headers.","difficulty":2}], passingScore: 70 },
      cheatSheet: [{"label":":","value":"Ends Python header lines"},{"label":"Indentation","value":"4 spaces = Python code block"},{"label":"_","value":"Underscore for snake_case"}]
